          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1341,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:a2-54:block:1",
          "start": 654
        },
        "quote": "(b) Notwithstanding subsection (a) , in recognition that the City Attorney represents the municipal corporation rather than any one Governing Body member or employee and that conflicts may arise, prior to appointment, the City Manager shall give the Governing Body a meaningful opportunity to provide input on the City Manager’s proposed appointee for City Attorney. Additionally, the City Manager cannot remove the City Attorney unless approved by the Governing Body. In accordance with Charter Ordinances 94 §11 and 96 §3 as codified in Section A2-25 of the Topeka Municipal Code, the Governing Body shall have no unilateral removal power of the City Attorney. (C.O. 124 § 2, 6-11-24.)",
